            "text": "No. Concrete pavers are engineered to perform unsealed for decades, and no manufacturer requires sealing as a warranty condition. Their durability depends on the base, edge restraint and jointing rather than a surface coating. Sealing is a cosmetic and maintenance choice with genuine benefits and genuine ongoing costs."
